SUMMARY:The Extraordinary Caterpillar (Greensboro)
DESCRIPTION:Join NCWF Triad Wild! Chapter for a joint event with T. Gilbert Pearson Audubon Society at the Greensboro Science Center. We will be screening the documentary The Extraordinary Caterpillar\, a beautifully shot 60-minute documentary that reveals the vital —and often overlooked—role caterpillars play in our ecosystems. \nFrom blooming meadows to city parks to backyard gardens\, this inspiring film celebrates the magic of nature while showing families practical ways to make a difference. Along the way\, you’ll see the groundbreaking work of The Caterpillar Lab\, entomologists David Wagner and Doug Tallamy\, co-founder of Homegrown National Park. This is a chance to see nature in a whole new light and to be part of the movement to bring it home. We hope you’ll join us! \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/the-extraordinary-caterpillar-greensboro/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/caterpillar.jpg
END:VEVENT
