SUMMARY:Herps & Habitats - Education & Exploration (Gatesville)
DESCRIPTION:Join NCWF Wildlife Habitat Stewards of Northeastern NC Chapter and Jeff Hall\, NCWRC’s Statewide Herpetologist\, for a hands-on mini workshop that dives into the fascinating world of the reptiles and amphibians of northeastern NC\, and why they are vital to North Carolina’s ecosystems and cultural heritage. \nYou will discover why herps (reptiles and amphibians) matter more than you think\, how to share our land with them\, tips to reduce human-herp conflicts\, and simple changes you can make to welcome herps to your property. \nFollowing the workshop\, we’ll head out for a guided group walk through Merchants Millpond State Park\, where we’ll search for herps in their natural habitat and see firsthand how their habitat essentials are met.  \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/herps-habitats-education-exploration-gatesville/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/herpsmmsp.jpg
END:VEVENT
