SUMMARY:Hanging Rock State Park – From Reservoir to Ridgeline (Danbury)
DESCRIPTION:Join NCWF Triad Wild Chapter and log your last summer hike at Hanging Rock State Park (and hopefully spot some early signs of autumn during the last weekend of summer!) \nThis 3-mile hike shows off some of the lesser-hiked parts of one of North Carolina’s oldest state parks. With a 429-foot elevation change\, hikers are encouraged to consider the climb and descent. The hike will be worth it; ascending among the boulders\, hikers are rewarded with views overlooking Winston-Salem\, Greensboro\, and even High Point visible on a clear day! \nAs hawk and raptor migration couples with fall bird migrations\, bird activity will be near its peak. Birders may get to catch a last glance of summertime birds like the summer tanager\, black-and-white warbler\, and great-crested flycatcher while hawks and falcons pass overhead! Leaves will begin showing signs of fall colors to come\, with the green peaks and valleys of summer still visible before the cold season kicks off. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/hanging-rock-state-park/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/septemberbirding.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC Wildlife Federation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260921T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260921T140000
DTSTAMP:20260819T184122Z
CREATED:20260819T184121Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260819T184122Z
UID:10001751-1789983000-1789999200@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:Great Coharie River Tree Tour (Clinton)
DESCRIPTION:Join NCWF and the Alliance for Cape Fear Trees for a guided tour of the Great Coharie River. Once logged extensively\, the Coharie River still has many large swamp chestnut oaks\, pine\, and bald cypress trees. The tour includes beaver dams\, winding blackwater channels\, and a tour of the Coharie tribal center with a 650-year-old dugout canoe. Come for the trees and leave with a deeper understanding of indigenous ecological stewardship. Ages 13+ \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/great-coharie-river-tree-tour-clinton/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/ACFTCoharieRiver.jpg
END:VEVENT
